1
00:00:00,422 --> 00:00:03,592
(Amy:)Homespun stories, knowledge
of physics and a bosom that defies it.

2
00:00:03,759 --> 00:00:06,299
(Amy:)You're the whole package,
aren't you?

3
00:00:07,554 --> 00:00:10,934
Sorry I'm Iate. Ugh, I got great news.

4
00:00:11,099 --> 00:00:14,939
(Howard(arriving):)NASA picked my team's design
for the deep field space telescope...

5
00:00:15,103 --> 00:00:17,563
(Howard(arriving):)...that's going on the
International Space Station this spring.

6
00:00:17,731 --> 00:00:19,481
Oh, woo, heh.
wow, heh.

7
00:00:19,649 --> 00:00:21,989
- Howie, that's wonderful! Congratulations!
Uh, heh.

8
00:00:22,152 --> 00:00:25,242
(Howard:)It gets better. Someone has
to go up with the telescope...

9
00:00:25,405 --> 00:00:30,115
(Howard:)...as a payload specialist,
and guess who that someone is, heh.

10
00:00:30,285 --> 00:00:32,495
Muhammad Li.

11
00:00:34,164 --> 00:00:35,874
Who's Muhammad Li?

12
00:00:36,041 --> 00:00:38,631
Muhammad is the most
common first name in the world...

13
00:00:38,794 --> 00:00:40,374
...Li, the most common surname.

14
00:00:40,545 --> 00:00:44,045
(Sheldon:)As I didn't know the answer, I thought
that gave me a mathematical edge.

15
00:00:45,217 --> 00:00:48,427
(Howard:)It's me, Sheldon. It's me.
I'm going up in space!

16
00:00:48,595 --> 00:00:50,885
(Howard:)Technically, I'm an astronaut.

17
00:00:51,056 --> 00:00:52,806
Oh, my God.
That's amazing.

18
00:00:52,974 --> 00:00:54,854
- Heh.
- Hang on a second.

19
00:00:55,018 --> 00:00:56,518
NASA doesn't have a shuttle anymore.

20
00:00:56,686 --> 00:00:58,776
- How are you gonna get up there?
- Oh, uh, it's cool.

